# Weave CBT Alembic

Alembic owns the PostgreSQL schema for the local CBT runtime.

`env.py` imports `app.model_registry` before reading `Base.metadata`, so every durable SQLAlchemy model must be imported by `app/model_registry.py`. Autogenerate and `alembic check` therefore see academics, auth, questions, exams, candidates, attempts, results, audit, and sync tables.

The domain model files under `app/domains/*/models.py` are the canonical SQLAlchemy model definitions. Alembic uses that metadata when generating a revision; committed revisions are then immutable schema history and must not import the live application models. `0001_initial_schema` is the static baseline for the current pre-launch schema. Any future model change must be represented by a new Alembic revision rather than editing `0001`.

Run Alembic from `backend/`:

```bash
alembic upgrade head
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe schema change"
alembic check
alembic current
alembic history
```

The database URL comes from application settings (`DATABASE_URL`). `alembic.ini` intentionally contains only a placeholder URL; `env.py` replaces it at runtime.
